{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013KoZXvQdQRQQGTvngWfqZ1","type":"tool_result","content":"diff --git a/jumping_pad/jumping_pad.gd b/jumping_pad/jumping_pad.gd\nindex 696ec05..841d509 100644\n--- a/jumping_pad/jumping_pad.gd\n+++ b/jumping_pad/jumping_pad.gd\n@@ -1 +1,39 @@\n extends Area3D\n+\n+## Launch speed applied along the pad's surface normal, tuned well beyond the\n+## player's own jump so the pad always sends them higher than they could\n+## manage unassisted.\n+const LAUNCH_SPEED := 28.0\n+\n+## How far the cap squashes down the instant it's hit.\n+const SQUASH_SCALE := Vector3(1.3, 0.55, 1.3)\n+const SQUASH_DURATION := 0.06\n+## Bouncy rebound back to rest, overshooting past the normal shape.\n+const REBOUND_DURATION := 0.6\n+\n+@onready var _mushroom: Node3D = %mushroom\n+\n+var _squash_tween: Tween\n+\n+\n+func _ready() -> void:\n+\tbody_entered.connect(_on_body_entered)\n+\n+\n+func _on_body_entered(body: Node3D) -> void:\n+\tif not body is Player:\n+\t\treturn\n+\tvar launch_direction := global_transform.basis.y.normalized()\n+\tbody.launch(launch_direction * LAUNCH_SPEED)\n+\t_play_bounce_visual()\n+\n+\n+func _play_bounce_visual() -> void:\n+\tif _squash_tween:\n+\t\t_squash_tween.kill()\n+\t_mushroom.scale = Vector3.ONE\n+\t_squash_tween = create_tween()\n+\t_squash_tween.tween_property(_mushroom, \"scale\", SQUASH_SCALE, SQUASH_DURATION) \\\n+\t\t.set_trans(Tween.TRANS_SINE).set_ease(Tween.EASE_OUT)\n+\t_squash_tween.tween_property(_mushroom, \"scale\", Vector3.ONE, REBOUND_DURATION) \\\n+\t\t.set_trans(Tween.TRANS_ELASTIC).set_ease(Tween.EASE_OUT)\ndiff --git a/player/player.gd b/player/player.gd\nindex a29ca01..e798958 100644\n--- a/player/player.gd\n+++ b/player/player.gd\n@@ -198,6 +198,15 @@ func shoot() -> void:\n \tbullet.global_position = origin\n \n \n+## Instantly overrides the character's velocity, discarding any existing momentum.\n+## Used by external triggers (e.g. jump pads) that need a real physics response\n+## -- gravity, air control and collisions still apply normally afterwards --\n+## rather than a scripted position change.\n+func launch(new_velocity: Vector3) -> void:\n+\tvelocity = new_velocity\n+\t_character_skin.jump()\n+\n+\n func reset_position() -> void:\n \ttransform.origin = _start_position","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0f97edbb-168e-425f-909f-c9f8a974a648","uuid":"9457e14b-79c9-4ac1-a7e8-ca467af065f9","timestamp":"2026-07-12T22:40:45.075Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"diff --git a/jumping_pad/jumping_pad.gd b/jumping_pad/jumping_pad.gd\nindex 696ec05..841d509 100644\n--- a/jumping_pad/jumping_pad.gd\n+++ b/jumping_pad/jumping_pad.gd\n@@ -1 +1,39 @@\n extends Area3D\n+\n+## Launch speed applied along the pad's surface normal, tuned well beyond the\n+## player's own jump so the pad always sends them higher than they could\n+## manage unassisted.\n+const LAUNCH_SPEED := 28.0\n+\n+## How far the cap squashes down the instant it's hit.\n+const SQUASH_SCALE := Vector3(1.3, 0.55, 1.3)\n+const SQUASH_DURATION := 0.06\n+## Bouncy rebound back to rest, overshooting past the normal shape.\n+const REBOUND_DURATION := 0.6\n+\n+@onready var _mushroom: Node3D = %mushroom\n+\n+var _squash_tween: Tween\n+\n+\n+func _ready() -> void:\n+\tbody_entered.connect(_on_body_entered)\n+\n+\n+func _on_body_entered(body: Node3D) -> void:\n+\tif not body is Player:\n+\t\treturn\n+\tvar launch_direction := global_transform.basis.y.normalized()\n+\tbody.launch(launch_direction * LAUNCH_SPEED)\n+\t_play_bounce_visual()\n+\n+\n+func _play_bounce_visual() -> void:\n+\tif _squash_tween:\n+\t\t_squash_tween.kill()\n+\t_mushroom.scale = Vector3.ONE\n+\t_squash_tween = create_tween()\n+\t_squash_tween.tween_property(_mushroom, \"scale\", SQUASH_SCALE, SQUASH_DURATION) \\\n+\t\t.set_trans(Tween.TRANS_SINE).set_ease(Tween.EASE_OUT)\n+\t_squash_tween.tween_property(_mushroom, \"scale\", Vector3.ONE, REBOUND_DURATION) \\\n+\t\t.set_trans(Tween.TRANS_ELASTIC).set_ease(Tween.EASE_OUT)\ndiff --git a/player/player.gd b/player/player.gd\nindex a29ca01..e798958 100644\n--- a/player/player.gd\n+++ b/player/player.gd\n@@ -198,6 +198,15 @@ func shoot() -> void:\n \tbullet.global_position = origin\n \n \n+## Instantly overrides the character's velocity, discarding any existing momentum.\n+## Used by external triggers (e.g. jump pads) that need a real physics response\n+## -- gravity, air control and collisions still apply normally afterwards --\n+## rather than a scripted position change.\n+func launch(new_velocity: Vector3) -> void:\n+\tvelocity = new_velocity\n+\t_character_skin.jump()\n+\n+\n func reset_position() -> void:\n \ttransform.origin = _start_position","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ccxy8QspwQbL7RJWPMgzU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Mushroom Jump Pad is implemented. Summary of changes:\n\n**`player/player.gd`** — added a small public `launch(new_velocity)` method that overwrites the character's velocity outright (discarding momentum) and triggers the jump animation. It's a pure addition; no existing logic changed, so gravity, air control, and collision response all continue through the normal `_physics_process`/`move_and_slide` path.\n\n**`jumping_pad/jumping_pad.gd`** — the previously empty script now:\n- Listens for `body_entered` and filters with `body is Player`, so enemies/projectiles/anything else pass through untouched (verified: a non-player `CharacterBody3D` fell straight through with unaffected velocity).\n- Launches the player along the pad's own up vector (`global_transform.basis.y`) at a fixed speed (28, vs. the player's normal jump impulse of 12), so flat pads send the player straight up and tilted pads send them up-and-outward, always at the same total strength regardless of incoming momentum (verified in headless tests: sprinting+falling into a flat pad still produced an exact `(0, 28, 0)`; a 30°-tilted pad produced `(0, 24.25, 14.0)`, same magnitude).\n- Plays a squash-then-elastic-rebound tween on the mushroom's scale on every contact, killing/restarting any in-flight tween so repeated bounces re-trigger cleanly (verified the scale overshoots past 1.0 before settling back to exactly `Vector3.ONE`).\n\nTested via a headless Godot run driving the actual `Player` and `JumpingPad` scenes (no editor-only mocks), confirming physics-correct launches, momentum discarding, tilt direction, visual rebound, and player-only filtering. Temporary test harness files were removed afterward — working tree only contains the two intended script edits."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1295,"cache_read_input_tokens":72822,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1295,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0f97edbb-168e-425f-909f-c9f8a974a648","uuid":"1927fc60-a69c-40ff-9c3a-581a6f4f1c3b","request_id":"req_011Ccxy8PGqLNs4njW162y1F"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":321035,"duration_api_ms":317217,"ttft_ms":1866,"ttft_stream_ms":1506,"time_to_request_ms":425,"num_turns":43,"result":"The Mushroom Jump Pad is implemented. Summary of changes:\n\n**`player/player.gd`** — added a small public `launch(new_velocity)` method that overwrites the character's velocity outright (discarding momentum) and triggers the jump animation. It's a pure addition; no existing logic changed, so gravity, air control, and collision response all continue through the normal `_physics_process`/`move_and_slide` path.\n\n**`jumping_pad/jumping_pad.gd`** — the previously empty script now:\n- Listens for `body_entered` and filters with `body is Player`, so enemies/projectiles/anything else pass through untouched (verified: a non-player `CharacterBody3D` fell straight through with unaffected velocity).\n- Launches the player along the pad's own up vector (`global_transform.basis.y`) at a fixed speed (28, vs. the player's normal jump impulse of 12), so flat pads send the player straight up and tilted pads send them up-and-outward, always at the same total strength regardless of incoming momentum (verified in headless tests: sprinting+falling into a flat pad still produced an exact `(0, 28, 0)`; a 30°-tilted pad produced `(0, 24.25, 14.0)`, same magnitude).\n- Plays a squash-then-elastic-rebound tween on the mushroom's scale on every contact, killing/restarting any in-flight tween so repeated bounces re-trigger cleanly (verified the scale overshoots past 1.0 before settling back to exactly `Vector3.ONE`).\n\nTested via a headless Godot run driving the actual `Player` and `JumpingPad` scenes (no editor-only mocks), confirming physics-correct launches, momentum discarding, tilt direction, visual rebound, and player-only filtering. Temporary test harness files were removed afterward — working tree only contains the two intended script edits.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session